  "preamble": "Loss of retroflexion turns [ɖ] into a plain alveolar or dental [d]. Assamese merged the inherited dental and retroflex stop series into a single alveolar series, and eastern (Dhaka) Bengali likewise shifts retroflex stops to alveolars; outside Indo-Aryan, Malay and Indonesian adapted Sanskrit retroflex ḍ in loanwords as plain d.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deretroflexion, Merger",
