          "from": "Sanskrit ḍāla [ɖaːla] 'branch'",
          "to": "ডাল dal /dɑl/ 'branch'",
          "note": "Historically the dental and retroflex series merged into alveolar stops in Assamese."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Bengali (Dhaka dialect)",
      "languageFamily": "Eastern Indo-Aryan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Rarh (western) Bengali ডাল /ɖal/ 'branch'",
          "to": "Dhaka Bengali /dal/",
          "note": "Eastern Bengali dialects shift retroflex stops to alveolars while keeping a contrast with dentals."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Malay",
      "languageFamily": "Malayic",
      "examples": [
